QUESTION
--------
The 2026-06-16 mpi-cpu pass (intermediate binary, OLD 7-term residue formula
A2r = A2-A1-A2x-A2s-A2c-A2l-A2o, which folded MYDUMP/ESCAPE/CHECK INTO A2r) saw
the ADJUST residue "A2r" explode ~12x from np1->np8 (0.57 -> 6.71 s asis;
0.76 -> 9.13 s adj4x). Roadmap suspects (XVPRED/CORE/LAGR/serial sweeps) were
all < 0.2 s -> refuted. Hypothesis: the blow-up is MYDUMP COMMON-dump I/O, made
8-way disk-contended by the per-rank-dir test harness (NBODY_RANK0_IO=0, every
rank writes the full ~100s-of-MB dump), and it vanishes under the production
rank-0 I/O guard (NBODY_RANK0_IO=1, only rank 0 writes).

The current binary (fcce9d4) breaks A2d (MYDUMP, phase 23) out as its own timer
and uses the 10-term residue (A2r now EXCLUDES A2d/A2e/A2k), so it can attribute
the blow-up to a single sub-phase. This run measures BOTH I/O modes:
  io0 : NBODY_RANK0_IO=0, per-rank dirs   -> every rank writes its own dump
  io1 : NBODY_RANK0_IO=1, ONE shared dir  -> only rank 0 writes (production)

